{"game": "elden-ring-nightreign", "language": "english", "appid": 2622380, "month": "2025-08", "window": 1, "start_date": 1754006400, "end_date": 1754611199, "month_true_total": 3786, "quota": 15, "returned": 15, "pulled_at": "2026-10-04 23:46:24 UTC", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "201670469", "author": {"steamid": "76561198406497179", "personaname": "黄文峰", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/ilickthighs/", "num_games_owned": 207, "num_reviews": 13, "playtime_forever": 11655, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 5647, "deck_playtime_at_review": 3, "last_played": 1784490279, "avatar": "e953d4b03ab78ace7a56cf2b714c4af72e038e94"}, "language": "english", "review": "grain", "timestamp_created": 1754610767, "timestamp_updated": 1754610767, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": false, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1748555952", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "201670146", "author": {"steamid": "76561198002478718", "personaname": "The Filthy Spaniard", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198002478718/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 3, "playtime_forever": 2415, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 1728, "last_played": 1755553261, "avatar": "1cf673264830a8295b11cae9473d21060e04e922"}, "language": "english", "review": "Don't buy this game if you intend to play it solo, it's ass. You might think, \"oh how bad can it be? I enjoy Elden Ring challenge runs after all\". Well, if you don't enjoy speed running, and enjoy the kind of challenge that rewards perseverance, then you will not enjoy this game. And before the \"git gud\" morons chime in, I've beaten all the night lords solo. It was not an enjoyable challenge, and the runs I was successful in were those which I got lucky with an overpowered setup and melted them without even having to learn their moves.\r\n\r\nIf you liked Elden Ring because of the exploration and combat, this game is not for you, as you have no time to fight anything or go anywhere that's not 100% required for the pathing that you must work out by looking at icons on the map in the first 20 seconds as you fly into the map. If you try to just organically explore the map and learn what to look for, you'll run out of time and find yourself in a multi-opponent boss fight dramatically under-levelled and under-geared. Looking up where to go and what to do is essential, so if you get any enjoyment through discovery, well you can kiss that goodbye too. \r\n\r\nIf you enjoyed Elden Ring's boss fights, and just want to try out the new fights in Nightreign, well there's only 8 of them, and I hope you enjoy a 30 minute run-back. And as mentioned, the runs where you get to the final boss easily will be where you've lucked into a strong build and didn't run into any roadblocks or delays. As a result, about half of them I beat on the first try.\r\n\r\nOn the flip side, the game is laughably trivial with a 3 stack of coordinated players, as even with increased enemy health pools, you can bum rush the bosses and chain stagger them to death. If you forget to dodge and get downed by one attack that your crew didn't manage to stagger the boss out of, your buddies can just revive you trivially. On the other hand, if you die solo (even with the character that has summons that could conceivably revive you like an ally would) you'll instantly die for real, and as well as dropping your runes, also lose a level. \r\n\r\nFinally, even if you get past all of that, the game fails as a roguelike because there's a pathetic amount of variation - I guess that's necessary seeing as the main challenge of the game is deciding a path and knowing where to go. Each type of location has 2 or 3 variants, with the same enemy placements, loot locations, and boss. Some locations will have some more variation in bosses, although it is still a very small pool, of just the repeated bosses from base game Elden Ring - none of the remembrance bosses, only 2 of the bosses from the Shadow of the Erdtree (no weapons, spells, or other enemies from that DLC are included for some reason). There are 6 bosses from previous souls games, and of them only Dancer of the Boreal Valley and Nameless King are worth writing home about. A bunch of \"boss fights\" are just a big pack of repeated base game enemies. Wildly, even the variants of the base game bosses aren't in the game - there's a fire dragon, and a frost dragon, but the magic, rot, ghostflame etc dragons are no where to be seen. The map geography is always the same except that sometimes on of 4 \"Shifting earth\" events will happen altering a portion of the map - but those are EXACTLY THE SAME each time you encounter one, so they essentially take away from the randomness rather than adding to it.\r\n\r\nIn summary, if you liked Elden Ring for any of the things it did best, skip this game that wears its skin but has none of its soul.", "timestamp_created": 1754610359, "timestamp_updated": 1754610359, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 1, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.47750285267829895", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1748555952", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "201669957", "author": {"steamid": "76561198343945563", "personaname": "gaslighter", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/mintedcopper/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 36, "playtime_forever": 18405, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 3674, "last_played": 1789774176, "avatar": "3d5697153ebe216054fa076b05fc1aa6ca58c8ee"}, "language": "english", "review": "very good", "timestamp_created": 